.TH Path.can_read 3 2026-09-01 "Tomo man-pages"
.SH NAME
Path.can_read \- check read permissions
.SH LIBRARY
Tomo Standard Library
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.BI Path.can_read\ :\ func(path:\ Path\ ->\ Bool)
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Returns whether or not a file can be read by the current user/group.


.SH ARGUMENTS

.TS
allbox;
lb lb lbx
l l l.
Name	Type	Description
path	Path	The path of the file to check. 
.TE
.SH RETURN
`yes` if the file or directory exists and the current user has read permissions, otherwise `no`.

.SH NOTES
This answers about the moment it is asked, and another process can change it immediately after. Do not use it to decide whether an operation will succeed: attempt the operation and handle its `Failure` instead.

.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
assert (/usr/include/stdlib.h).can_read()
assert not (/etc/shadow).can_read()
assert not (/non/existant/file).can_read()
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR Tomo-Path (3)
